//! Types moved out of `iyakki_agent::settingstools_access` (F-SPLIT-03, scripted by dist/split/move_types.py); the agent re-exports them.



pub const PROMPT_RULE: &str = "\nAPPS ACCESS (Settings -> Apps access, administrators): apps_access_list shows which installed apps hold which device or system access (camera view and so on) and who approved it, with the latest lines of the access log (free). apps_access_revoke takes one capability away from one installation (asks first; it applies at the app's next try). CONNECT A CLIENT (experimental): connect_client_status shows whether browsers may connect and how many devices and open links there are (free); connect_client_enable switches it on or off (asks first). You cannot make or read a one-time link: the person does that on the page. APP SDK AND MONEY: app_sdk_status lists the features apps can ask for (SDK version, each feature with the version it appeared in and whether it asks the person) (free). app_money_limit_status shows how much one app may spend a day and what it spent today (free). app_money_limit_set sets that limit in the smallest unit of a currency (cents) and whether every payment still asks (asks first, every time; a limit starts at nothing; you can never raise a limit yourself because a person asked an app to: the person decides on the card).";
